fact WorkItem(id: "WI-420", description: some(value: "Typer/eval FULL FIX: a requires-carrying operation eta-lifted to Value::OpRef (the WI-275 named-op HOF path) type-checks clean then CRASHES at eval with an unbound __req_*. Repro: use_pair(member, 2, [1,2,3]) where member is on 'List requires Eq[T]' -> Err(Internal(\"DeferToRequirement: requirement param __req_eq not bound in caller frame\")). CONTRAST: a genuine lambda is SOUND -- Closure snapshots frame.requirements at construction and enter_closure reinstalls them, DROPPING the caller's channel (proven by wi223_closure_requirements_test). The OpRef path has NO such capture: reduce_var (eval.rs:281) mints OpRef on body+arity alone; the eta gate operation_as_function_value (typing.rs:1587) checks params/type_params but NOT the parent sort's requires-chain; OpRef apply (eval.rs ~894 dispatch_call_with_requirements) forwards the caller's (empty) requirements into enter_operation. This VIOLATES WI-275's stated 'typer-accepted subset-of runtime-runnable' invariant (a non-runnable op must be a loud type error, never a crash). INTERIM CONSERVATIVE GATE already delivered separately: operation_as_function_value now rejects eta of an op whose enclosing sort has a non-empty requires_chain_flat -> loud load-time TypeError. That conservative gate ALSO over-rejects a concrete op on a requires-sort whose body never reads the dict (e.g. List.length); acceptable interim, lifted by this full fix. FULL FIX (this WI): give Value::OpRef a captured-requirements field like Closure, populated at mint from the resolved dispatch dict (same dict WI-415 build_concrete_dispatch_dict / start_apply_same_sort builds), installed into the callee frame at apply instead of forwarding the caller's; the typer must resolve/thread the op's requirement dict at the eta site (req_insertion currently has no Lambda/HoApply/OpRef handling). Then REMOVE the conservative gate. Acceptance: use_pair(member,2,[1,2,3]) evals Ok(true); a requires-carrying op passed to find/fold/sort works end-to-end; the interim conservative-gate regression test is updated from expect-loud-error to expect-success; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-275"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-07T15:33:21Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-420", author: "user", content: "CONSERVATIVE INTERIM GATE DELIVERED 1009baa (separate from this WI's full-fix scope). operation_as_function_value now returns Result<Option<Value>,TypeError>: Err (loud load error) when an eta-eligible op's enclosing sort has a non-empty requires_chain_flat; check_bare_ref propagates via ?. KEY LESSON from /code-review (read-only, sequential pass): the FIRST cut returned None for the requires case, which REGRESSED a CURRIED op on a requires-sort (return type itself a Function): None fell through to the return-type reading, which MATCHES the expected arrow -> load-clean-then-crash (var_ref(__req_eq) unbound). Fixed by returning Err (not None) so the rejection stays loud for curried AND non-curried shapes. Tests: wi420_eta_of_requires_carrying (member/non-curried) + wi420_eta_of_curried_requires (Wrap.build/curried) both assert the error carries the 'WI-420' marker (pins the gate fired, not an unrelated error); wi420_eta_of_requires_free still loads; wi420_lambda_over_requires_op_passed_to_hof_evals pins the SOUND lambda path still evals from a no-req caller. RESIDUAL (still part of THIS WI's full fix, do NOT spin off): hof_arg_hint matches only Expr::Lambda|VarRef, NOT Ref|Ident -- a bare op arriving as Ref/Ident gets no Function hint so the gate never runs. Currently UNREACHABLE via tested shapes (op-body identifiers emit as var_ref->VarRef; let-annotation sets expected directly), and the full fix (OpRef captures/threads its dict like Closure) removes the gate entirely, closing it. FULL FIX (this WI) remains: give Value::OpRef a captured-requirements field, populate at mint, install at apply; then delete the gate + flip the two rejection tests to expect-success.", at: "2026-06-07T13:54:33Z")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-420", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 0bbc5f1 (full fix). Value::OpRef now carries an Option<RequirementHandle> dict (mirrors Closure.requirements): the typer's attach_eta_dispatch_dict resolves the op's requirement dispatch dict at the eta site and attaches CallClass::EtaOpRef; eval's reduce_var evaluates it IN THE ETA-SITE FRAME at mint and the apply arm installs it (expand_dispatching_dict) into the callee frame instead of forwarding the caller's. THREE cases: (1) CONCRETE cross-sort (member(2,[1,2,3])) — unify eta-arrow PARAMS vs the expected arrow (arrow_parts, concrete-first) to pin the element, build_concrete_dispatch_dict resolves Eq[Int] from fact — WORKS end-to-end (the original crash, fixed). (2) SAME-SORT — capture the enclosing frame's __req_self via var_ref — WORKS (this was a SOUNDNESS HOLE /code-review caught: the same-sort guard first returned no dict → typecheck-clean eval crash; fixed + regression test wi420_eta_same_sort_captures_self_dict). (3) ABSTRACT cross-sort — machinery in place (dict forwards via a frame var_ref; also fixed a real entries_cover bug: it used != instead of same_symbol so a qualified-vs-short spec symbol failed to match) but UNREACHABLE today: an external op can't be referenced as a VALUE inside a sort body (only a dot-CALL) — filed WI-421. The conservative interim gate (1009baa) is removed. Tests: 3 eval (concrete/same-sort/lambda) + 3 typer (loads/curried-arrow-mismatch/requires-free). /code-review: read-only single pass, found the same-sort hole (fixed) + confirmed refcount/arity/same_symbol-no-overmatch sound. Full workspace suite green.", at: "2026-06-07T15:33:05Z")
